<title>GERMANY: SGL Carbon Q1 pre-tax profit down 9 pct.</title>
<headline>SGL Carbon Q1 pre-tax profit down 9 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WIESBADEN, Germany 1997-05-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 31</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   43	vs 48</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     71	vs 78</p>
<p>    Group operating profit		   80	vs 80</p>
<p>    Group DVFA earnings per share	  2.01    vs 2.28 marks</p>
<p>    Group sales				  452     vs 411</p>
<p>    Group return on sales		    18 pct  vs 19 pct</p>
<p>    Group gross cash flow		    73	vs 78</p>
<p>    Group tax ratio			    39 pct  vs 38 pct</p>
<p>    Balance sheet total			1,789   vs 1,433</p>
<p>    Equity ratio				 43 pct  vs 39 pct</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German carbon and graphite maker is SGL Carbon AG. The company said it had expected a weak start to the year because of several one-off factors and weakness in the European steel industry. Referring to the decline in pretax profit, the company noted that first-quarter earnings were burdened by the cost of management share schemes, lower income from non-consolidated companies and increased interest payments resulting from acquisitions.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
